Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["CausalHeight", "ObjectName",
 CellID->1224892054,ExpressionUUID->"8393d601-4014-44ba-afc9-60862df940ec"],

Cell[TextData[{
 Cell["   ", "ModInfo",ExpressionUUID->"a949e9ae-0fcb-4acc-bc10-f1aaa27ffbc8"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{
   TemplateBox[{
     Cell[
      TextData["CausalHeight"]], 
     "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/CausalHeight", 
     "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
    "PackageLink",
    BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"], "[", 
   StyleBox["g", "TI"], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "c7235fdb-ae3b-410a-8846-70955a2d0466"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "gives the causal height of every event of the directed acyclic graph ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ": the number of edges of a longest chain from a source to it, zero exactly \
on the sources.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"0529cf94-334a-4736-93a6-4123b2be0ea3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Definition: the causal height of an event ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " is ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = max over the sources ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " below ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " of \[Tau](",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), the number of edges of a longest chain from ",
 StyleBox["s", "TI"],
 " to ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "; on a source ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 " = 0. Equivalently ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") = 1 + max ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 ") over the direct predecessors ",
 StyleBox["u", "TI"],
 " of ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ", which is how it is computed, in one pass over a topological order."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"54172117-7ec3-49c9-b93d-0e6645a15525"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A time function on a causal graph is an integer function that increases \
along every edge. The causal height is the least one that is nonnegative: any \
other such function ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 " satisfies ",
 StyleBox["f", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") \[GreaterEqual] ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 "), by induction along a longest chain. It needs no observer and no choice; \
its level sets are the slices ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSlice"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/InfraSlice", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5c22c86a-c32d-4613-a3cb-bd7a13ebc521"],
 " of the height foliation ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["CausalHeightFoliation"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraCausality/ref/CausalHeightFoliation", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraCausality Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "c0513bb3-76ce-44bf-a706-7ae92e911879"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"a53179a0-c050-40d9-96bb-7ea5d92072f1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The result is an association ",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 " \[RightArrow] ",
 StyleBox["t", "TI"],
 "(",
 StyleBox["v", "TI"],
 ") over the events of ",
 StyleBox["g", "TI"],
 ", in the order of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"VertexList", "[", "g", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "62b3dac4-43d2-412d-a03f-324f89eab07a"],
 ". It is a density in the sense of InfraGeometry: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["InfraSubstrateHighlight"]], 
    "paclet:WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry/ref/InfraSubstrateHighlight", 
    "WolframInstitute/InfraGeometry Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "dde4a5e2-c764-4f90-b41b-09d6d7d52355"],
 " draws it, a source with value 0 left plain."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"841eb48d-564f-4241-b148-27cbf5f68037"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The longest chain from a source is the discrete proper time of the observer \
that started at the beginning: on a geodesic observer from a source, the \
causal height of the ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 "-th tick is ",
 StyleBox["m", "TI"],
 " \[Minus] 1. On the diamond lattice the causal height of (",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ") is ",
 StyleBox["i", "TI"],
 " + ",
 StyleBox["j", "TI"],
 ", twice the coordinate time; on the cylinder lattice it is the row."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"e15291b3-cc56-48c5-a9d2-0a7faa482352"],

Cell["Corresponding notions:", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"0cdf8fcf-20f7-4949-9ebd-16fcd5c0c94b"],

